    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2 tests, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the registration-date rule on `POST /api/owners`: when no `registrationDate` is supplied it defaults to the server's current date, and it's returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `registrationDate` property (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Because `Owner` composes `OwnerFields` via `allOf`, this field is both accepted on create (`OwnerFieldsDto`) and returned on read (`OwnerDto`). The OpenAPI `format: date` generates a `LocalDate`, which Jackson serializes as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a persisted `LocalDate registrationDate` field (`@Column(name = \"registration_date\")`) with getter/setter. MapStruct auto-maps it by name in both directions, so `OwnerMapper` needed no changes.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 After mapping the incoming DTO to an `Owner`, defaults the registration date to `LocalDate.now()` when it's null, before saving. A supplied date is preserved.\n\n4. **DB schemas** \u2014 Added the `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table in all four schema files (hsqldb \u2014 used by tests \u2014 plus h2, mysql, postgres for consistency).\n\nBoth acceptance tests pass: `coreDefaultsToToday` (omitted \u2192 today) and `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate` (`2020-06-15` preserved).",
